.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store

# Generated images are build output, not source. The brief and the prompt
# sidecar are what get committed; regenerating from them is the point.
# Remove this line if a specific approved asset should be versioned here.
briefs/*/out/
out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working files. Local, iterative, and not part of the toolkit.
#
# Everything below is real and useful; none of it is something a stranger who
# clones this repo should have to read or carry. docs/workspace.md is committed
# and explains what belongs in each of these, so the flow can be rebuilt without
# the files themselves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Session state. Read at the start of a session, written before the end.
PROGRESS.md

# Reading notes on harness and design method. Ours, and about how we work
# rather than about how the toolkit works.
docs/foundations.md
docs/harness-map.md
docs/breakdowns.md

# Third party templates, downloaded verbatim. Not ours to redistribute.
docs/templates/

# Context for this particular portfolio, in Portuguese. Nothing here is needed
# to use the toolkit.
reference/

# Drafts, posts and contact sheets about the work.
docs/writeups/

# Two lessons that are ours rather than the toolkit's. Both are about which
# accounts to buy and when, no committed code depends on either, and the part
# worth keeping is already a hard constraint in CLAUDE.md.
docs/solutions/free-credit-is-a-hypothesis.md
docs/solutions/subscription-is-not-api-credit.md

# The archive of what each round of iteration produced.
docs/history/*
!docs/history/README.md
